<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>That changeless Christ is still as near</l><l>And just as kind and strong to save;</l><l>He came to lift our fallen race</l><l>From sin and sickness and the grave.</l><l>As in the days of Galilee,</l><l>Disease still flees at His command;</l><l>But ere His touch your frame can feel,</l><l>You, too, must still stretch forth your hand.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>What though you feel so weak and faint?</l><l>He can your will with strength endue,</l><l>New faith and courage breathe within</l><l>And work in you to will and do.</l><l>Reach out to meet His quickening touch;</l><l>Take up your bed, arise and stand;</l><l>And pressing through to meet your Lord,</l><l>Stretch forth your hand, stretch forth your hand.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
